  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Love Love Love** (2 reviews, 1 other source): The track labeled banter on the matrix recording begins with talk but is mostly Love Love Love; The uploader missed adding Love Love Love to the track labels and said it would be fixed [1][3][4]\n- **The Plague** (1 other source): The uploader's notes list The Plague as an unreleased song [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Jeff Davis County Blues**: back after 83 archived shows (1627 days) [5]\n- **Damn These Vampires**: back after 66 archived shows (1328 days) [5]\n- **The Plague**: rare: 8 archived performances [5]\n- **Isaiah 45:23**: rare: 13 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2022-05-02** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 22 songs; 91 min; rated 2.5/5 by 2 [1]\n- **tmg2022-05-02.aud.mv88.flac24**: audience recording; 22 songs; 92 min [2]. Said about its sound: The stage lip had almost no PA coverage, so the recording has a very drum and bass heavy mix [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: No Children, missing Matt Douglas, song decision, tech issue [1]\n- The taper recorded from the stage lip, directly in front of the bass [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2022-05-02**: taped by me; transferred by me; source: CA-14 (healy on stage) > CA-Ugly 2 > PCM-A10 + SBD [Engineer: Brandon Eggleston] > PCM-A10 [1]. Also: The taper puts banter on separate tracks so listeners can easily skip it, for example on playlists while exercising [4]\n- **tmg2022-05-02.aud.mv88.flac24**: taped by One Dozen Cats; source: MV88 > iPhone 8 > WAV (24/48) [2]. Also: Recorded with an MV88 into an iPhone 8 as 24/48 WAV, edited in REAPER, then converted to 24/48 FLAC [2]",
